  "_migration_note": "Repointed from legacy 'Fybroc Attributes and Constraints.xlsx' MAIN sheet to authoritative 'Fybroc Configuration Rev0.3.xlsx' Selections sheet. Rev0.3 uses Question/Answer columns (B/C) with a three-state validity matrix across 10 series columns D..M (1500..8500): STD=standard default, X=selectable option, blank=not selectable. The series_constraint_compiler records is_standard=true for STD markers so the configurator can pre-select defaults and part-number generation can apply the standard-value marking. Verified marker counts in Rev0.3: X=1905, STD=195, blank=4670. Replaces the legacy value-per-series columns E..O and F_* field codes. See docs/evidence/F120/FYBROC_SELECTIONS_MODEL.json."
